_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-07T13:04:32Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "5. This minor planet in the main belt holds a notorious spot in the history of astronomical nomenclature. Discovered in 1971, it was the first asteroid named after a character from a cult-classic—but with a twist. The discoverer technically named it after his pet cat, who happened to share a name with the logical, pointed-eared Science Officer of the USS Enterprise. The International Astronomical Union was so frustrated by this \"backdoor\" tribute to fiction that they subsequently banned the naming of asteroids after pets.", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-07T13:04:47Z", "username": "Abhishek Saluja", "text": "Spock", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-07T13:04:49Z", "username": "Nikhil Borra", "text": "Spock", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-07T13:04:49Z", "username": "Abhishek Vats", "text": "Spock", "role": "chat", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-07T13:04:59Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Spock is correct", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-07T13:05:09Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "Sal 38 Vats 10 Nikhil 2", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}, {"timestamp": "2026-04-07T13:06:09Z", "username": "Kartikey Pradhan", "text": "next:", "role": "elaboration", "is_correct": null, "has_media": false, "media": null}]